<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Supremes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1839–1842</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Supremes was a civil war in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-new-granada">Republic of New Granada</a>, present-day Colombia and Panama, from 1839 to 1842. It began as a revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasto">Pasto</a> against the closure of small convents and spread as regional strongmen, the 'supreme chiefs', rose against the government of José Ignacio de Márquez. The government won with generals Pedro Alcántara Herrán and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-cipriano-de-mosquera">Tomás Cipriano de Mosquera</a>, and the conflict shaped the later Liberal and Conservative parties.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-supremes.jpg" alt="War of the Supremes" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Walhouse Mark · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cerca_de_Bogot%C3%A1,_milicias_neogranadinas,Edward_Walhouse_Mark,_1843.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
